==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|liable|ity}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/laɪəˈbɪlɪti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-liability.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|li|abil|ity}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Liability}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[obligation]], [[debt]] or [[responsibility]] owed to someone.
#: {{cot|en|asset}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1901|author=w:W. W. Jacobs|title=w:The Monkey's Paw|text="I was to say that Maw and Meggins disclaim all responsibility," continued the other. "They admit no '''liability''' at all, but in consideration of your son's services they wish to present you with a certain sum as compensation."}}
## {{lb|en|accounting}} Any item recorded on the [[right-hand]] side of a [[balance sheet]].
##: {{ant|en|asset}}
# A [[handicap]] that holds something back, a [[drawback]], someone or something that is a [[burden]] to whoever is required to take care of them; a person or action that [[expose]]s others to greater [[risk]].
#: {{cot|en|asset}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2016 January 31|url=http://www.vanityfair.com/news/2016/01/huma-abedin-hillary-clinton-adviser|title=Is Huma Abedin Hillary Clinton’s Secret Weapon or Her Next Big Problem?|journal=Vanity Fair|text=Asked if at some point Huma becomes a '''liability''' to Hillary, the long-term Clinton insider replies, “It’s like anything else. I don’t think so, but you know I don’t have any idea. Hillary is very loyal, but she’s obviously pragmatic.”}}
## {{lb|en|informal|mildly|derogatory}} A person on a team that is more of a [[hindrance]] than a [[help]].
##: {{ux|en|You're a bloody '''liability''' sometimes!}}
# The [[likelihood]] of something happening.
# The condition of being [[susceptible]] to something.

